  "method": {
    "build": "From separate clean directories run scripts/build_native_eiffel.ps1 -BuildTier Production and -BuildTier Assertions. Both use the x64 MSVC backend. Only production DLLs timed.",
    "harness": "Stock benchmarks/fair_speed/fair_speed.c, cl /O2 /Z7 /link /INCREMENTAL:NO /DEBUG:FULL /OPT:REF /OPT:ICF /MAP. Each timed parse includes parser creation, all XML_Parse calls and parser free. File I/O is outside the timer.",
    "collection": "6 rounds for 16 configurations. One warm-up per engine and configuration, with ceil(160 ms / warmup ms) parses per timed measurement, clamped to [1, 250]. Random.Random(11024 + zero-based round).shuffle permutes case order. The three engine orders rotate through the six permutations for every case. Checksums and acceptance validated for every run.",
    "repeat": "python reports/windows-dll-latin1-checkpoint-2026-11-24/repeat_timings.py --harness <fair_speed.exe> --before <before.dll> --after <after.dll> --expat <libexpat.dll> --out <new-directory>",
    "timing_summary": "Median elapsed milliseconds per parse for each engine. Speedup is the median of paired before/after time ratios across rounds on the same case. Absolute times depend on compiler, CPU and load.",
    "counters": "Counters came from a separate finalized build with stderr probes at the Latin-1 decoder, full-document, prefix, cached DOCTYPE and continuation calls. Each case ran once. Raw decode counts measure bytes passed to the decoder and parser counts measure UTF-8 bytes passed to parser entry points. The stock DLLs provided all timings.",
    "oracle": "Declared and explicitly selected Latin-1, with a valid document and a mismatched end tag, accented text/attribute data, CRLF, whole input, all two-part splits, byte-by-byte and explicit empty final calls. Compared status/error, failure call, joined text events, and (byte,line,column) at start/end callbacks and completion. All 214 direct traces were also compared against the XML_GetBuffer/XML_ParseBuffer traces."
  },
